The core theoretical contribution—the decision calibration collapse to minimax-optimality of plug-in best response—is a genuine advance that upgrades prior swap-regret guarantees. The framework is clean, the duality characterization is computationally tractable, and the practical instantiations connect to real training pipelines. The paper's main limitations are the approximate calibration gap (not analyzed in the main body) and narrow experiments. Relative to the 6.75-scoring QA-calibration paper (similar theory-to-practice ratio), this paper has a somewhat stronger conceptual insight (the collapse result) but weaker empirical validation, placing it in a comparable range. Relative to the 7.5-scoring higher-order calibration paper, this paper has somewhat less depth in the theoretical development but a cleaner main message.

