InnoGym sits between Agent-as-a-Judge (5.67, which had human validation) and ST-WebAgentBench (4.25, which had limited scope). It is stronger than the truly weak papers (MPG at 1.5, planning benchmark at 2.0) due to its genuine contributions in problem framing and benchmark construction. But it is weaker than papers that validated their metrics (CREATIVITY INDEX at 7.0) or had thorough experiments (DataEnvGym at 7.5). The unvalidated novelty metric is a significant gap for a paper whose central contribution is measuring innovation, and the overclaiming about results compounds this. I score at 4.5, near the lower end of the borderline range.

