The paper under review sits firmly in the medium range. It has a genuine empirical contribution (comprehensive benchmarking, practical finding that NF-SLT works well on tabular data) and interesting analytical work (d Ratio, dimensionality analysis), but the definitional shift from likelihood inversion to relative performance is a significant concern that undermines the paper's strongest claims. The theoretical contribution is limited by unrealistic assumptions. Compared to papers that redefine phenomena and overclaim (meta-OCL at 5.25, zero-shot OD at 5.75), this paper has more empirical substance but a similar core weakness. It's better than papers with purely theoretical overclaiming (NCGAMI at 3.0) but not at the level of comprehensive empirical studies with solid theoretical grounding (SSL evaluation at 8.0).

